{"A Petroff, in which Mr Le Patourel (Oxford), on the 6th move, prematurely
sacrificed two minor pieces for a Rook, for no adequate compensation in attack;
on the contrary, Mr. Lester soon assumed the offensive, and brought the game
to an early conclusion..." - a possible opening sequence which fits the known
facts leading up to this position might be 1 e4 e5 2 Nf3 Nf6 3 Bc4 Bc5 4 Ng5
0-0 5 0-0 h6 6 Nxf7 Rxf7 7 Bxf7+ Kxf7 8 d3 Kg8 9 Kh1 Nc6 10 f4 d6 11 h3 exf4
12 Rxf4 Qe7 13 Qe1 Bd7 14 c3 Ne5 15 Qe2 Ng6 16 Rf3 Nh5 but this is pure
speculation - JS} 17. g4 Bxg4 18. hxg4 Qh4+ 19. Qh2 Qe1+ 20. Kg2 Qe2+ {Source:
The Field, 6 April 1889, p480} 0-1

